== dispatch points
ok the source is attached
ok Open
ok Next
ok Last
ok Next at the end (no move)
ok Prior
ok First
ok MoveBy
ok MoveBy(0)
ok RecNo
ok GotoBookmark
ok Locate, found
ok Locate, not found
ok Edit
ok a field write
ok UpdateRecord
ok Post
ok Insert
ok Cancel
ok Append
ok navigation posts a modified record
ok CheckBrowseMode cancels an unmodified record
ok Delete
ok Refresh
ok Filter without Filtered
ok Filtered
ok Filter while Filtered
ok FilterOptions while Filtered
ok Filtered off
ok FocusControl
ok a field is moved
ok Close
== several data sources
ok every source is notified, in the order of attachment
ok each event goes to all sources before the next event
ok detached
ok a detached source gets nothing
ok attached again: now last
ok a destroyed source is detached
ok destroying the dataset detaches its sources
== DisableControls
ok enabled at first
ok ControlsDisabled
ok DisableControls itself sends nothing
ok the events of the dataset still fire; no data event is sent
ok editing while disabled
ok nothing reached the data sources
ok the operations themselves worked (the refresh reloaded the rows)
ok enabled again
ok EnableControls: the state is the same, the data changed
ok EnableControls fires no dataset events, only the data event
== EnableControls: what is sent
ok nothing was suppressed: nothing is sent
ok the state changed meanwhile: deUpdateState first
ok events flow again
ok the state is the same as at DisableControls: no deUpdateState
== nesting
ok one EnableControls of two: still disabled
ok and nothing is sent yet
ok the second EnableControls enables
ok and notifies once
ok EnableControls without DisableControls does nothing
ok the counter never went below zero
ok one EnableControls is enough
== closed dataset
ok closed while disabled
ok DisableControls works on a closed dataset
ok Open while disabled sends nothing
ok opened while disabled
failed checks: 0
